Z||000042||DaRkLoRD||06-27-2001||09:28 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-508s.jpg">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Could a decklid scoop be used for further cooling? maybe something else besides the Mustang one, something rounded that would fit better with the Finale/Fino styling.. btw, I really love the back end.. the hatchback was cool, but this looks like a more evolved version of the GT.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>     <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 06-27-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000043||Archie||06-27-2001||09:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KissMySSFiero:<BR><B>so the fino rear clip uses the stock decklid vents?   can you use either the gt or the coupe style  vents?  <P>are you going to have any cars with the original finale hatch?  I like the hatch better because i like to see the engine.  <P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You need to use the Coupe vents.<P>Yeah, I like the hatch too. Especially when I have a V-8 in the car. I like to call it "Chevy under glass".<P>The car we are painting this week (yes, yet another one) has the Fino nose and the Hatchback style rear clip &, of course a SBC engine.<P>Archie||||reg||1
